# Jenga tower: a giant Jenga tower 11.4 m tall and 3 m square, eighteen layers of three pale birch blocks (each 3 x 0.6 x 1 m),
# every layer turned a quarter turn on the one below, every block nudged a little off true. A game well under way: from the sixth
# to the thirteenth layer eight blocks are pulled out, some from the sides and some from the middle, so slots and tunnels open
# right through the tower at mid-height to see and shoot through, and two of them are laid crosswise on top.
format 1
collider mesh

# Half the vertices its size would give it: big, simple forms, and dozens of game pieces lie on the board
Detail detail=0.5
    Material material=jenga_wood
        Union
            # Layer 1, blocks along x
            Translate translation=(-0.021, 0.3, -1.0)
                Rotate rotation=(0, -0.0175, 0)
                    RoundBox size=(1.48, 0.298, 0.48) roundness=0.06
